# picsl_greedy 1.4.0, linux aarch64. Kitware publishes the VTK wheel-SDK for x86_64
# only, so greedy has to build VTK from source on arm64 and no aarch64 wheel is
# published to PyPI; these are built out-of-band from the same 1.4.0 sources.
#
# What these digests are for: they pin *which bytes* the arm64 image installs, so the
# wheels can be mirrored to a release under this project's control without anyone having
# to take the mirror on trust -- a mirrored copy either hashes the same or the build
# fails. Regenerate only when GREEDY_VERSION in docker/Dockerfile changes:
#
#     sha256sum picsl_greedy-<version>-cp3XX-cp3XX-linux_aarch64.whl
#
# or read them from the release without downloading:
#
#     gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/releases/tags/<tag> --jq '.assets[] | "\(.digest)  \(.name)"'
#
2888611259ccca52a8d11fc966bee192aefbe6d12a3cc33ec2e6294328f053ac  picsl_greedy-1.4.0-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl
d22d949bf2ebbf2624ace47c575e3172594c98a3d4c42765d7ccef106646445a  picsl_greedy-1.4.0-cp311-cp311-linux_aarch64.whl
4490d3dadf792227ef7e696b04173f519f4843bd9b3e0688b71e4d977eb2ae64  picsl_greedy-1.4.0-cp312-cp312-linux_aarch64.whl
d156036e1885b69df17bc2f79ac9c3e12c46f13e88e5e6eb4b7efa3dedf73fd8  picsl_greedy-1.4.0-cp313-cp313-linux_aarch64.whl
